    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1505.03237v1</id>
    <title>Geometrically Nilpotent Subvarieties</title>
    <updated>2015-05-13T04:37:41Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.03237v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1505.03237v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We construct some examples of polynomial maps over finite fields that admit subvarieties with a peculiar property: every geometric point is mapped to a fixed point by some iteration of the map, while the whole subvariety is not. Several related open questions are stated and discussed.</summary>
